#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""The approval gate: every public post is shown to the owner first, and publishes itself after 15 minutes if he decides nothing.

That second clause is the whole guarantee and this line used to omit it -- it
read "nothing reaches a public Telegram surface without the owner pressing
Confirm", which stopped being true on 2026-09-13 when auto-deliver was added
at his request (01fc08e). The gate fails OPEN now, not closed. An item that
goes out that way is recorded "auto after N min, NOT reviewed" and is never
merged with a real approval, so "who approved this?" still has an answer.
Set APPROVE_AUTO_SECONDS=0 to go back to failing closed.

WHY THIS EXISTS, in the owner's words (2026-09-13):

    "every automatic message to public channel or group should be send to my
     personal bot @PCoinPCNBot and there should be 2 button confirm and cancel,
     if i confirm then it should be sent to destination, otherwise ill cancel,
     this is for security so the admin AI model if go mad, then nothing be
     posted publicly until i confirm"

That is a threat model, not a preference, and it is the right one. There is now a
model in this estate that composes text and posts it to a public group by itself.
Its output filter is good. It is still a model, and the blast radius of a bad
minute is the project's public reputation. A human confirm button caps that at
"the owner saw something odd in a DM".

THE FIVE PROPERTIES THIS FILE IS BUILT AROUND. Each is here because the obvious
implementation would have got it wrong:

1. FAIL CLOSED. Every failure path -- unreadable queue, unreadable config, an
   unparseable item, a Telegram error -- refuses to publish. Nothing here may
   ever resolve an unknown into "go ahead". A gate that opens when it is confused
   is not a gate.

2. THE APPROVED BYTES ARE THE PUBLISHED BYTES. What the owner sees in the DM is
   the real message, and a SHA-256 of it is stamped on the item at submit time
   and re-checked immediately before publishing. If anything edits the queue
   between approval and publication -- the exact move a compromised or
   malfunctioning process would make -- the hash disagrees and the item is
   refused, loudly. Approving a preview and publishing something else is the one
   failure this design exists to make impossible.

3. THERE IS NO BYPASS. No --yes, no --force, no auto-approve, no environment
   variable that skips the DM. A caller can only ever move an item to `pending`.
   Only a callback carrying the owner's own Telegram user id can move it to
   `confirmed`, and only `confirmed` items publish. Adding a bypass flag later
   would defeat the entire file, so there is deliberately no hook to hang one on.

4. DESTINATIONS ARE AN ALLOW-LIST, NEVER A PARAMETER. The caller passes a NAME
   ("channel", "group"), not a chat id. pcoin-announce hardcodes the public
   channel id for exactly this reason: an id that arrives as an argument is an id
   an attacker -- or a confused model -- can change, and the ops channel has been
   posted to publicly once already.

5. A MAD PROCESS MUST NOT BE ABLE TO FLOOD THE OWNER. A model in a loop would
   otherwise submit thousands of approval requests and the DM becomes unusable,
   which is a denial of the approval mechanism itself. MAX_PENDING caps it; over
   the cap, submissions are refused and ops is told once.

EXPIRY is the fifth property's quieter cousin: an item nobody decides within
EXPIRE_HOURS can never be published. A week-old approval sitting in a queue is a
loaded gun -- circumstances have moved on, and "he said yes on Tuesday" is not
consent to publish on Sunday.

USAGE
    pcoin-approve submit --dest group --text "..." [--reply-to MID] [--source NAME]
    pcoin-approve submit --dest channel --photo card.png --text "..." [--key K]
    pcoin-approve list [--all]
    pcoin-approve show ID
    pcoin-approve decide --id ID --decision confirm|cancel --by TELEGRAM_USER_ID
    pcoin-approve tick          # DM anything pending, publish anything confirmed
    pcoin-approve selftest      # exercises the state machine, sends nothing
"""
